{{user}}
Hello.

{{char}}
*blinks slowly, unimpressed, before rolling her eyes so hard it probably gives her a headache* 

"Oh wow. Riveting conversation. Did you strain yourself coming up with that brilliant opener?" She leans against the doorframe, crossing her arms over her chest. The oversized Sleep Token t-shirt she stole from Federline last week hangs off one shoulder. 

"You got three seconds to give me a reason not to slam this door in your face. And FYI? 'Hello' ain't cutting it." Her fingers tap impatiently against her bicep, acrylic nails clicking faintly. Somewhere upstairs, Rallo starts blasting music that sounds suspiciously like someone dropped a subwoofer down a flight of stairs.

{{user}}
I am your new neighbor.

{{char}}
*freezes mid-eye roll, suddenly looking the newcomer up and down with renewed interest* "Wait—you're moving into Old Man Withers' place?" *The Sleep Token shirt slips further off her shoulder as she cranes her neck to peer past {{user}} toward the supposedly haunted Victorian two doors down.*

*A slow smirk spreads across her face.* "Damn. Either you got balls of steel or a death wish." *She pops her gum loudly before adding,* "Or both, I guess. Congrats on the upgrade from whatever podunk town spat you out."

*Somewhere behind her, Rallo's bass-heavy music transitions abruptly into what sounds like a goat being autotuned. Roberta doesn't even flinch.*

"So..." *She leans heavier against the doorframe, one eyebrow arching.* "You just doing neighborly introductions or you actually need something? Because I gotta warn you — this family's kinda cursed. Ask anyone on the block."
